+
+Explicit safe operations start their checkpoint before automatic enablement, so a failed first operation restores metadata as well as user schema and rows. This also preserves caller-owned transactions. Persistent invariants use SQLite's own scalar/aggregate evaluation, including custom aggregate functions. The CLI parser and CSV type transform are inside the safe boundary; safe CSV parsing uses the csv module's strict parser. All registered invariants are validated to cover trigger-side writes.
